00:00:46.429 --> 00:00:47.801
(laughing)
- Oh my god.

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:48.634
What a treat.

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:50.860
- I'll take it but totally a lie.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:52.370
Your accent reminds me of home,

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:53.750
I always love when I run into you.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:54.960
Like it just feels...

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:56.160
So where did you grow up?

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.360
- I grew up in North Carolina.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:00.020
My mom made me be a debutante,

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:01.110
that's how southern I am.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:01.943
- [Kelly] You're a southern belle.

00:01:01.943 --> 00:01:02.776
- I am.

00:01:02.776 --> 00:01:03.609
- You're a southern belle.

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:05.393
Wait, what did that entail?
What did you have to do?

00:01:05.393 --> 00:01:06.880
Oh my gosh!

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.320
- I was like, what happened?!

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.410
(audience laughing)

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.840
- You are so fancy right now.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.050
- [Fortune] Yeah I had to
wear a white wedding gown.

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.180
- [Kelly] Oh my god, you
were from the bricks.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:17.013
I was from the sticks,

00:01:17.013 --> 00:01:18.390
girl, we didn't have anything like that.

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:21.000
- Listen, but we had no money.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.830
That was the thing, my mom had been one

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.727
and then we lost all our money.

00:01:24.727 --> 00:01:25.560
(laughing)

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:26.727
It happens.

00:01:26.727 --> 00:01:27.738
- It happens.

00:01:27.738 --> 00:01:29.797
- You know, gambling and...

00:01:29.797 --> 00:01:31.297
(laughing)

00:01:31.297 --> 00:01:33.870
And then she still wanted me to carry on

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:37.820
this tradition of pretending to be rich

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:40.862
and then go to etiquette classes.

00:01:40.862 --> 00:01:41.804
- That's amazing.
- [Norman] Etiquette classes?

00:01:41.804 --> 00:01:43.854
- Yeah I had to learn how to be a lady.

00:01:43.854 --> 00:01:46.414
(laughing)

00:01:46.414 --> 00:01:48.404
No I didn't know, I didn't know.

00:01:48.404 --> 00:01:49.447
- [Kelly] I don't.
- I had to like,

00:01:49.447 --> 00:01:52.033
dab my face with a napkin.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.517
You can't wipe your face like a monster!

00:01:55.517 --> 00:01:57.270
(laughing)

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:59.470
- Obviously I didn't
attend etiquette class.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.150
- Well still to this day,

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:04.090
people are like, you
should never eat in public

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.327
'cause it's not great.

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:08.420
- So what did your family think whenever

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.250
you told them you were gay?
'Cause being from the south

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.120
that is not always an easy conversation.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:15.040
- Yeah, I mean I think my mom for her

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:18.050
she just, she didn't
want my life to be harder

00:02:18.932 --> 00:02:21.970
than what life can be.
- Already.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:25.060
- Already but we had this
really poignant moment,

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:27.010
I talk about it in my special

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:30.270
where I told her I was gay
and she was stone faced

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:33.023
and I was like oh man,
does she hate me now?

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:38.262
She was like, we are goin' to Hooters!

00:02:38.262 --> 00:02:41.020
(laughing)

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:42.840
I was like what!

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:45.300
So that was her way of being,

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.734
I accept you, let's go to Hooters.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:50.150
(laughing)

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:52.400
And then when I told my dad,

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.400
he was like, he's very
typical southern man

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.443
that's very simple and he's like, okay.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:04.360
All right, well you wants us
to buy you a men's blazer?

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:07.242
(laughing)

00:03:07.242 --> 00:03:09.231
Or a top hat?

00:03:09.231 --> 00:03:12.250
(laughing)

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:13.460
Lesbians don't wear top hats.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:14.430
- I love your dad.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:16.650
In his mind, like if women like women

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:17.910
you wanna dress like a man.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:19.043
- For sure.

00:03:19.043 --> 00:03:21.843
He was like, okay let's get
you that top hat and blazer.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:24.430
- That's kind of amazing though.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:25.960
Being from the south
that they were accepting

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:28.360
'cause I know a lot, I have
a lot of friends actually,

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:30.970
or few friends that they
didn't say let's go to Hooters

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:32.140
they said let's go to church

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.800
and they wanted to pray for 'em and like

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.390
change 'em straight or something

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.550
and I'm like, I don't
think your prayers gonna

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.419
make 'em straight, just sayin'.

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:42.030
Yeah so it can be hard for people.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.560
- A hundred percent, I mean

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:45.320
we've come a long way
but there's still plenty

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:48.300
of people who are
disowned by their families

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.520
and I'm so lucky that my family--

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:51.353
- [Kelly] Your parents, they're awesome.

00:03:51.353 --> 00:03:53.480
- Yeah they were just like,
we love you no matter what.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:56.610
You are no different
than you were yesterday.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:57.988
And I mean, yeah.
- That's so good.

00:03:57.988 --> 00:03:58.821
That's so good.

00:03:58.821 --> 00:03:59.654
(audience clapping)

00:03:59.654 --> 00:04:00.487
- Yeah.

00:04:00.487 --> 00:04:04.030
